# Motion

Authored motion uses the `--motion-*` tokens in `src/shared/styles/tokens.css` and nothing else. Documented in `specs/tokens/token-reference.md`.

- Durations, easings, springs, distances, blur, press scale, and stagger come from those variables.
- Do not add a raw duration or a `cubic-bezier()` outside `tokens.css`.
- `linear` is allowed only for real time (spinner, loading pulse, countdown, progress) and for the damped error shake. Loading pulse duration is `--motion-duration-pulse`.
- `--motion-ease-ios` is reached only through `--motion-nav-*` and `--motion-sheet-*`. Do not put it on components.
- `--nav-parallax: 30%` is the iOS page spatial constant in `navigation.css`. Do not copy it onto other components.
- `--motion-spring-bouncy` is one confirmed-success element per screen. Errors do not bounce.
- Reduced motion swaps movement for a fade at `--motion-duration-sm` and `--motion-ease-standard`. It does not delete feedback. Stagger, parallax, and shake are removed.
- Do not animate height, width, or `left` / `top`. Use transform and opacity.
